- All four REPL turn entry points (regular prompt, \`!N\` history, clipboard paste, image) now go through \`prepareTurnCheckpoint\`. There's no remaining bare \`createCheckpoint\` before \`runInteractiveTurn\`.
- The behaviour matches the sidecar flow merged in #147:
  - an explicitly read-only launch skips the checkpoint and clears any fallback;
  - a successful checkpoint clears the fallback;
  - only a \`SensitivePersistenceError\` triggers the prompt, and every other error is re-thrown as before;
  - choice 3 is the only path to \`allowSensitive: true\`;
  - 4 and 5 don't start the turn;
  - an invalid entry re-prompts and never picks a default.
- The tests cover each choice's proceed/fallback/retry outcome, the re-prompt, the read-only launch, and sticky read-only followed by resume once a later safe checkpoint succeeds.

**Note:** if an earlier turn chose option 1 (read-only) and a later turn chooses option 2, the fallback isn't cleared, so 'the current mode' still means read-only. The sidecar does the same and it matches the sticky-until-a-safe-checkpoint semantics, but the option-2 wording could say 'current (possibly read-only) mode'. The checkpoint-error exposure on the history, paste and image paths is the same as before this PR, since those calls weren't wrapped previously either.

